anv: H.264 HuC BRC patches the slice states too (SLBB layout as media-driver, gen125+)

media-driver puts the slice states behind the image-state group in the BRC second level batch (AvcHucBrcUpdatePkt::
ConstructImageStateReadBuffer: image group + BBE, cache line aligned, then per slice MFX_AVC_SLICE_STATE +
VDENC_AVC_SLICE_STATE + BBE; UPD_SLBB_Size = aligned image group, UPD_NumSlicesForRounding = slices) and runs each
slice's group from the kernel's output (AvcVdencPkt::SendSlice), so the HuC applies its QP dependent rounding to the
slices. ANV kept the slice states in the primary batch. The output slice groups are seeded with the driver's own
first, so the PAK always runs complete states.
1080p60 VBR 3/6/12 Mbit/s against x264 medium: Netflix Aerial BD-rate +10.5% -> +9.2% (PSNR-Y), +17.7% -> +16.3%
(VMAF); DrivingPOV +30.6% -> +29.9%, +12.7% -> +12.3%.

